Vivado 2025.2 DDR4 IP (mem_v1_4) speed limit patch: allow DDR4-2666 (tCK 750 ps) instead of
DDR4-2400 for single-rank DIMM/SODIMM (1 slot, 1 rank, DCI cascade off, bank group 1, Vnom) on
UltraScale+ -2 E/I, -2L C/E/I and -3 E. This runs the PL above the DDR4 rate AMD supports for these
speed grades - use at your own risk. Keep a copy of the original file before patching.

Apply from the Vivado install directory (e.g. C:/AMDDesignTools/2025.2/Vivado), git-bash or Linux:
    git apply -p1 <repo>/Patches/xilinx_mig/time_periods_2025.2.patch
or
    patch --binary -p1 -i <repo>/Patches/xilinx_mig/time_periods_2025.2.patch
Undo with "git apply -R -p1 ..." / "patch --binary -R -p1 -i ...". The CSV uses CRLF line endings, so
this file must keep its exact bytes (marked -text in .gitattributes); plain "patch" without --binary
fails in git-bash on Windows.

